      "mission": {
        "base_commit": "036462190bb0d65baf05110816f65c5939fa1d2a",
        "delegation_parent": "R/B",
        "depth": 1,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "Choosing the shorter matrix dimension for band pairs reduces work on rectangular inputs, while contiguous independent band-extension updates can be safely exposed to GCC vectorization. A small generation-stamped table also avoids per-band map allocation and clearing.",
        "id": "2fac1021e12d4c10",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "B",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/main.cpp"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Store the input in band-axis-first order, transposing logically when rows exceed columns, so band-extension updates traverse contiguous memory.",
            "Iterate band pairs along the shorter dimension and scan the longer dimension, maintaining compressed sums for each band.",
            "Apply GCC's ivdep only to the independent contiguous compressed-sum update loop.",
            "Replace the per-band unordered_map with a fixed-size open-addressed frequency table using generation stamps; retain signed 64-bit prefix sums and query before inserting each prefix."
          ]
        },
        "tree_id": "e1:B",
